          "status": "supports",
          "note": "Pokorny, IEW, Page(s): 881-882: 'Root/lemma: sāwel- sāwol- su̯uel-, su̯el-, sul-, Meaning: sun. Note: next to which su̯en-, sun-, thus of old n/n-stem'. Found in POK_full.txt at line 71617 ff. (grep -n 'sauel-'); the entry closes 'References: WP. II 446 f., WH. II 553 f. … Page(s): 881-882'. Exactly the page Nourai cites and exactly his headword."
        }
      ],
      "consulted": [
        {
          "src": "WLD",
          "where": "Walde-Pokorny, Bd. II pp. 446-447 (WLD_Bd2_pages.txt, line 29615)",
          "stance": "supports",
          "note": "'sāuel-, su̯uel-, su̯el-, sul- „Sonne“, woneben su̯en-, sun-, so daß sich sāu-, sū- als Wz., -el und -en als Stammbildungssuffixe ergeben.' Followed by 'ai. ved. suvar n. = av. hvarə „Sonne, Licht, Himmel“, gen. surah = av. hūrō'."
        },
        {
